    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "It would look something like this, which is not necessarily more readable IMO. Now we don't leverage the single-time index filtering. Besides, we reassign the iterator which might create some inconsistent behaviors. WDYT?\r\n\r\n```ts\r\nfunction resetPageFromWidgets(widgets: Widget[]): void {\r\n  let indexWidgets = widgets.filter(isIndexWidget);\r\n\r\n  while (indexWidgets.length > 0) {\r\n    indexWidgets.forEach(widget => {\r\n      const widgetHelper = widget.getHelper()!;\r\n\r\n      widgetHelper.overrideStateWithoutTriggeringChangeEvent(\r\n        widgetHelper.state.resetPage()\r\n      );\r\n\r\n      indexWidgets = widget.getWidgets().filter(isIndexWidget);\r\n    });\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nTo [compare with this](https://github.com/algolia/instantsearch.js/blob/063e5bef0e94357f5c5abac6594279680a285bb1/src/widgets/index/index.ts#L44-L61).",
